The scrollable URL
description: a fragment's address in the browser - the in-page `#` rule
- >
  A fragment is addressable in the browser by the in-page `#` rule (see
  `tools/server/README.md`): its node path `<material>/yo/fragments/<key>` becomes the
  scrollable URL `<material-url>#yo/fragments/<key>` - the `#` standing in for the `/` after
  the served material. Opening that URL (or clicking the fragment in the viewer's fragments
  panel) scrolls text/PDF/djvu regions into view and pans image/map regions to fit, then
  briefly flashes the region.
